---
import Post from "../../../layouts/Post.astro";
import NutritionNav from "../../../components/NutritionNav.astro";
import FoodRecordEntry from "../../../components/FoodRecordEntry.astro";
import record from "../../../data/nutrition/record.json";
import guide from "../../../data/nutrition/guide.json";
const guideEntry = record.entries.find((entry) => guide.record_href.endsWith(`#${entry.id}`));
const frontmatter = {
  title: "Food record",
  description: "The reported eating days, portions, appetite, taste and training behind my nutrition notebook.",
  updated: record.updated,
};
---
<Post frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <NutritionNav current="record" />
  <p>This is the growing eating record behind the <a href="/nutrition-notebook/">nutrition notebook</a>. It preserves food eaten, actually taken supplements and available observations about taste, appetite and training. Purchases, proposed meals and discarded leftovers retain their own status.</p>
  <p>The September diary supplies three dated, partial food reports and a described eating pattern. The later October reports were made around midnight; their reporting dates are known, while the calendar eating dates remain unconfirmed. Reported portions and quantities assumed for a calculation are displayed separately.</p>
  <p>The current <a href="/nutrition/guide/">nutrient guide</a> uses <a href={guide.record_href}>{guideEntry?.title ?? "the linked eating entry"}</a>. Its figures and attention judgments remain tied to that entry until reviewed again.</p>
  <h2 id="record-index">Entries</h2>
  <ul class="record-index">
    {record.entries.map((entry) => <li><a href={`#${entry.id}`}>{entry.title}</a><span class="dim"> — report received {entry.recorded_local_date}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  {record.entries.map((entry) => <FoodRecordEntry entry={entry} />)}
  <h2 id="background">Background and planned changes</h2>
  <p>These observations explain the progression. They are separate from the foods actually eaten on a particular day.</p>
  {record.background?.map((entry) => <details id={entry.id}>
    <summary>Recorded {entry.recorded_local_date}: {entry.kind.replaceAll("_", " ")}</summary>
    <p>{entry.summary}</p>
  </details>)}
  <h2 id="record-method">How a day is added</h2>
  <p>A new entry begins with the food actually eaten and its supported date. Counts and container sizes are useful; an edible weight is an estimate unless measured. Supplements enter totals only when taken. Taste, hunger and training can be recorded as observations without converting them into measured energy expenditure or recovery.</p>
  <p>The nutrient tables reuse a saved, sourced food catalog. A matching package label supplies known facts; generic food composition and recipe estimates retain their qualifications. A missing value is unknown rather than zero. New information can correct a quantity or product value, with the reason kept in the relevant entry.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/nutrition/guide/#nutrient-index">nutrient guide</a> explains what each estimate means. Repeated complete records can establish a more useful pattern; one day's table cannot measure nutrient stores or diagnose a deficiency.</p>
</Post>
<style>
  details { margin: 24px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  details[open] summary { margin-bottom: 20px; }
</style>
